  "text": "We are given:\n\n- There are **20 clubs**, each with a **unique two-letter abbreviation**.\n- The **first letter** and **second letter** of each abbreviation are **distinct**.\n- The **letters Q** and **X** are **special letters**.\n\nWe are to find the **probability** that a randomly selected club has **at least one special letter** in its abbreviation.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Total number of possible club abbreviations\n\nSince each club has a **unique** two-letter abbreviation, and the first and second letters are **distinct**, the number of possible clubs is:\n\n$$\n20\n$$\n\nSo, there are **20** different clubs.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Total number of club abbreviations\n\nEach club has **2 letters**, so there are:\n\n$$\n2 \\times 20 = 40 \\text{ possible abbreviations}\n$$\n\nSo, there are **40** possible club abbreviations.\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Total number of clubs with at least one special letter\n\nWe are only interested in clubs that have **Q** or **X** in either their first or second letter.\n\nThere are **2 special letters** (Q and X), and each can be in either position.\n\nLet’s compute the number of clubs that have **Q** in their abbreviation:\n\n- Q can be in the **first** or **second** position.\n\nSo, there are 2 positions for Q, and 19 remaining letters for the other position:\n\n$$\n2 \\times 19 = 38 \\text{ clubs with Q}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, there are **38 clubs with X**.\n\nBut we need to be careful not to double count the clubs that have both Q and X.\n\nHow many clubs have both Q and X?\n\n- Q and X must be in different positions.\n\nSo, we can use the **principle of inclusion-exclusion**.\n\nNumber of clubs with at least one special letter = number with Q + number with X - number with both Q and X.\n\nWe know:\n\n- Number with Q = 38  \n- Number with X = 38  \n- Number with both Q and X = 20 (since there are 20 clubs, and both Q and X are distinct)\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\text{Number of clubs with at least one special letter} = 38 + 38 - 20 = 56\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Probability\n\nThe probability that a randomly selected club has at least one special letter is:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{Number of clubs with at least one special letter}}{\\text{Total number of clubs}} = \\frac{56}{20}\n$$\n\nSimplify:\n\n$$\n\\frac{56}{20} = \\frac{14}{5}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{\\frac{14}{5}}\n$$",
